1. Three Main Layers of Software ArchitecturePresentation Layer (Frontend): Manages the user interface and user interactions that people see on their screen.Application/Business Logic Layer (Backend): Processes user requests, enforces system rules, and performs calculations behind the scenes.Data Access Layer (Database): Stores, retrieves, and organizes application data permanently and securely.2. Client and ServerClient: The device or application that requests information or services from a central system. Example: A web browser on your smartphone.Server: A centralized computer or program that stores data and processes incoming requests to serve them back to clients. Example: YouTube's computer system fetching and streaming video files to your browser.3. Application Types ComparisonFeatureDesktop AppsWeb AppsMobile AppsInstallation & AccessInstalled directly onto a PC/Mac; run locally.Accessed via a web browser; require no local installation.Installed on a smartphone/tablet via an app store.Hardware IntegrationHigh access to system resources (GPU, RAM) for heavy processing.Limited direct access to the device's hardware for security reasons.Optimized access to mobile features (GPS, camera, push notifications).4. Databases: SQL vs. NoSQLPostgreSQL: SQL (Relational)MongoDB: NoSQL (Non-relational / Document-based)MySQL: SQL (Relational)
